    "forensics": "The recent losses stem primarily from tight stop-loss whipsaws (0.55% - 0.65% price moves) triggered during mid-morning liquidity transitions (10:25\u201311:10 IST) in cyclical names like TATASTEEL and NTPC. Additionally, late-afternoon entries (13:55\u201314:20 IST) lacked sufficient time and momentum to reach the 1.15% target, resulting in stagnant EOD square-offs where statutory fees and brokerage flipped flat gross PnL into net losses. Overall, the system isgross-profitable (+\u20b925.72) in Phase 2, proving that execution friction (\u20b935.94 in fees) and premature stop-outs are the sole barriers to net profitability.",
    "learning": "In Indian NSE cash equities on a micro-capital base, gross profitability is easily eroded by statutory transaction charges unless initial stop-losses accommodate standard 5-minute intraday noise (requiring ~0.65%+ buffer) and profit targets are calibrated for higher hit rates before EOD square-off.",
